## Scenarios

### nogc_sync_mut platform path ownership

#### retains canonical path implementations through native entry closure

- Verify: retains canonical path implementations through native entry closure
   - Expected: source does not contain `path.normalize_path(input_path)`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: retains canonical path implementations through native entry closure")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
val source = file_read("src/lib/nogc_sync_mut/platform.spl")
expect(source).to_contain("export use nogc_sync_mut.path.{normalize_path, is_absolute_path, join_path}")
expect(source.contains("path.normalize_path(input_path)")).to_equal(false)
```

</details>

#### forwards path behavior without a runtime module object

- Verify: forwards path behavior without a runtime module object
   - Expected: normalize_path("alpha\\beta") equals `alpha/beta`
   - Expected: is_absolute_path("/tmp/simple") is true
   - Expected: join_path("alpha", "beta") equals `alpha/beta`


<details>
<summary>Executable SSpec</summary>

Runnable source: 5 lines folded for reproduction.
Reproduction: this block contains the complete executable scenario source.

```simple
step("Verify: forwards path behavior without a runtime module object")
# @req: REQ-SSPEC-LOCAL-001
expect(normalize_path("alpha\\beta")).to_equal("alpha/beta")
expect(is_absolute_path("/tmp/simple")).to_equal(true)
expect(join_path("alpha", "beta")).to_equal("alpha/beta")
```

</details>

